# Ex1 expectations, shared by the Python and R installed-distribution
# tests. Hand-derived from the fixture inputs (ex1.tab, ex1.rda) and the
# documented legacy defaults; not generated from a run of the code under
# test.
#
# The table is 3 size classes x 3 regions plus computed totals (16 cells).
# Every input cell carries the manual status S except (Stor, Nord), which
# is explicitly marked U in ex1.tab. With no SAFETYRULE in the batch, the
# manual status is the only source of unsafety.
#
# (Stor, Nord) = 150 is the manual primary suppression. The legacy default
# manual margin is 20% of the cell value, so its lower and upper
# protection requirements are both 30.
#
# CELL <row>;<col> <response> <status>   (status before suppression;
#                                         Total row/col come first)
CELL Total;Total 1080 S
CELL Total;Ost 465 S
CELL Total;Vest 360 S
CELL Total;Nord 255 S
CELL Liten;Total 100 S
CELL Liten;Ost 45 S
CELL Liten;Vest 30 S
CELL Liten;Nord 25 S
CELL Mellom;Total 290 S
CELL Mellom;Ost 120 S
CELL Mellom;Vest 90 S
CELL Mellom;Nord 80 S
CELL Stor;Total 690 S
CELL Stor;Ost 300 S
CELL Stor;Vest 240 S
CELL Stor;Nord 150 U
# PRIMARY <row>;<col> <response> <required_protection>
PRIMARY Stor;Nord 150 30
